.TH ct2util "1" "November 2018" "CheeseCutter-EXTended 0.3.1 utilities" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ct2util \- manual page for CheeseCutter-EXTended utilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ct2util
\fI\,<command> <options> <infile> <-o outfile>\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
CheeseCutter\-Extended 0.3.1 utilities, based on CheeseCutter 2.9.
.IP
ct2util import <infile> <infile2> <\-o outfile>
ct2util init <binaryfile> <\-o outfile>
.SS "Commands:"
.TP
prg
Export song (.ct) to PRG file
.TP
sid
Export song (.ct) to SID file
.TP
dump
Dump song data to assembler source (BETA)
.TP
import
Copy data from another song without overwriting the player
.TP
init
Create a fresh .ct from player binary
.TP
sid2ct
Convert a CheeseCutter 4.x .sid back to a .ct song (best effort: the song comes
back purged, without instrument names). Prints the detected player generation;
exits non\-zero for a SID that was not made with CheeseCutter.
.TP
sidtrace
Print the 25 SID registers (hex) after each play call of a .sid, one line per
call. Two traces are equal when the songs drive the SID identically.
.SS "General options:"
.TP
\fB\-o\fR <outfile>
Set output filename (by default gathered from input filename)
.SS "Export options:"
.TP
\fB\-r\fR <addr>
Relocate output to address (default = )
.TP
\fB\-d\fR <num>
Set the default subtune (1\-32)
.TP
\fB\-s\fR <num>
Export single subtune (1\-32) (disables \fB\-d\fR)
.TP
\fB\-zp\fR <num>
Relocate zero page (valid range 2\-)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR
Don't output information
.SS "sidtrace options:"
.TP
\fB\-s\fR <num>
Subtune to trace (1\-32, default 1)
.TP
\fB\-f\fR <num>
Number of play calls to trace (default 3000)
.PP
Prefix value options with '0x' or '$' to indicate a hexadecimal value.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccutter(1),
.BR klystrack(1),
.BR goattracker (1).
